THIRD-PARTY NOTICES

The decimated surfacelet transform reimplements, in Julia, the construction of
SurfBox, the reference toolbox of Y. M. Lu and M. N. Do (MATLAB File Exchange
14485): its Fourier-domain multiscale pyramid, its "ritf" hourglass filter bank,
its iterated resampled checkerboard (IRC) filter bank and its subband ordering.
SurfBox's source was consulted to reproduce that construction, and the golden
data under test/reference/ was produced by running SurfBox.  No SurfBox file is
included in this repository.  SurfBox carries the following notice, retained
here:

  SurfBox (c)
  A set of C++ and Matlab routines implementing the surfacelet transform in
  arbitrary N-dimensions (N >= 2)
  Yue Lu and Minh N. Do
  Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering
  Coordinated Science Laboratory
  University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign

  This software is provided "as-is", without any express or implied warranty.
  In no event will the authors be held liable for any damages arising from the
  use of this software.

The methods themselves are those of the published papers, cited in the source
files and listed in docs/src/theory.md, chiefly:

* Y. M. Lu and M. N. Do, "Multidimensional directional filter banks and
  surfacelets", IEEE Trans. Image Process. 16(4), 2007.
* Y. M. Lu and M. N. Do, "A mapping-based design for nonsubsampled hourglass
  filter banks in arbitrary dimensions", IEEE Trans. Signal Process. 56(4), 2008.

No code is derived from the MATLAB Contourlet Toolbox (GNU GPL) or the
Nonsubsampled Contourlet Toolbox (no licence stated).
